IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp5-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer (cp5-seat.l4): at least one for every question, in the facts a real person would state.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the text of the Act (and, where a question reads a regulation, from the
-- Regulations), before the code was run. A month is written as its first day. A day that a question ignores is `cp5 case -- a day that is not used`.
-- The people are invented: Mei (born 15 June 1960; reaches 60 in July 2020 and 65 in July 2025 under section 2(2));
-- Ben (born 15 June 1950); Noor (a survivor); a child born 15 June 2010.

§ `Cases for the seat`

-- A day the question ignores because the matching yes/no is no.
`cp5 case -- a day that is not used` MEANS YearMonthDay 2000 1 1

§§ `Retirement pension`

-- Mei applied on 10 September 2020, at 60; approved on 1 October 2020; chose no month; has not stopped working.
-- Section 67(3.1): the month after the application, October 2020.
#ASSERT `From which month is my retirement pension paid (s 67)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 10 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 9 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 10 1)
-- She chose January 2021: that month governs.
#ASSERT `From which month is my retirement pension paid (s 67)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 10 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 9 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 1 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1)
-- Not approved: the Act does not say from which month.
#ASSERT `From which month is my retirement pension paid (s 67)` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 9 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Ben applied on 10 September 2010 at 60 and is still working: his pension waits for 65 (July 2015) under subsection (2).
#ASSERT `From which month is my retirement pension paid (s 67)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 10 1) (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2010 9 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 7 1)
-- Ben, after 70, with the requirement to apply waived on 17 March 2023: April 2022 under subsection (3.2).
#ASSERT `From which month is my retirement pension paid (s 67)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 17) (YearMonthDay 1950 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 17) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 17) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 4 1)
-- A pension that started before 1987 (subsection (1)): born 15 June 1920, applied 10 May 1986, last worked and contributed December 1985: January 1986.
#ASSERT `From which month is my retirement pension paid (s 67)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1986 5 10) (YearMonthDay 1920 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 5 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 12 20) TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 12 1) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 1 1)
-- Section 68: Mei's pension is paid for August 2025 if she died on 31 August 2025 (the month of death), not for September.
#ASSERT `Is a retirement pension paid for a particular month (s 68)` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a retirement pension paid for a particular month (s 68)` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31))
#ASSERT `Is a retirement pension paid for a particular month (s 68)` (YearMonthDay 2040 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used`
-- Section 67(4): Mei's disability pension (applied for 12 March 2015; last payable August 2022) ended; notified 1 October 2022; she applied on 15 December 2022, within 90 days.
#ASSERT `In which month is my application for a retirement pension treated as received, after my disability pension stopped (s 67(4))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 12 15) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2015 3 12) (YearMonthDay 2022 8 20) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 8 1)
-- Out of time and no longer period allowed: not covered.
#ASSERT `In which month is my application for a retirement pension treated as received, after my disability pension stopped (s 67(4))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2023 1 15) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2015 3 12) (YearMonthDay 2022 8 20) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Disability pension and post-retirement disability benefit`

-- Mei became disabled in March 2020: the fourth month following is July 2020.
#ASSERT `From which month is my disability pension payable (s 69)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 12) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1)
#ASSERT `From which month is my disability pension payable (s 69)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 12) TRUE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1)
#ASSERT `From which month is my disability pension payable (s 69)` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 12) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How many months before my application can I be treated as having become disabled (s 69(b))` TRUE EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `How many months before my application can I be treated as having become disabled (s 69(b))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 70(1): nothing else happens, so the pension ends with the month of her 65th birthday, June 2025; if she ceased to be disabled in September 2022, that month.
#ASSERT `Until which month is my disability pension paid (s 70(1))` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 6 1
#ASSERT `Until which month is my disability pension paid (s 70(1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 9 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2022 9 1
-- Section 70(2): ends because she reached 65; the application for a retirement pension is treated as made in June 2025, to start in July 2025.
#ASSERT `Does my disability pension end because I reach 65 (s 70(2))` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my disability pension end because I reach 65 (s 70(2))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 9 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used`)
#ASSERT `In which month am I treated as having applied for a retirement pension when my disability pension ends at 65 (s 70(2))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1)
#ASSERT `From which month does the retirement pension I am treated as having applied for at 65 start (s 70(2))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)
#ASSERT `From which month does the retirement pension I am treated as having applied for at 65 start (s 70(2))` FALSE (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 70(3).
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying for a disability pension because I have started a retirement pension (s 70(3))` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I barred from applying for a disability pension because I have started a retirement pension (s 70(3))` TRUE TRUE)
-- Section 70.01.
#ASSERT `From which month is my post-retirement disability benefit payable (s 70.01)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 12) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1)
#ASSERT `From which month is my post-retirement disability benefit payable (s 70.01)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2018 12 20) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How many months before my application can I be treated as having become disabled, for a post-retirement disability benefit (s 70.01(b))` TRUE EQUALS JUST 12
-- Section 70.02: Mei reaches 65 for this section in July 2025 (the month after her birthday's month).
#ASSERT `Until which month is my post-retirement disability benefit paid (s 70.02)` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 7 1
#ASSERT `Until which month is my post-retirement disability benefit paid (s 70.02)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 9 3) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2024 9 1
-- 2007, c. 11, s. 36.
#ASSERT `Does the 25-year contribution test in subparagraph 44(2)(a)(i.1) apply to my application for a disability pension (2007, c. 11, s. 36)` (YearMonthDay 2008 2 20) (YearMonthDay 2008 2 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2007 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the 25-year contribution test in subparagraph 44(2)(a)(i.1) apply to my application for a disability pension (2007, c. 11, s. 36)` (YearMonthDay 2008 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2008 2 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2006 10 31))

§§ `Reinstatement`

-- Mei stopped receiving her disability pension in March 2020 because she returned to work; she became incapable again in March 2022 (24 months later).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to have my disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated (s 70.1(1); 2004, c. 22, s. 23)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2022 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1)
-- A person who stopped in March 2005, before section 20 of the 2004 Act came into force on 1 June 2005 (a stated input): excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to have my disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated (s 70.1(1); 2004, c. 22, s. 23)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2005 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2006 12 1) (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1))
-- Too late: 25 months.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to have my disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated (s 70.1(1); 2004, c. 22, s. 23)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2022 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1))
-- The request: made on 31 March 2023 for an incapacity in March 2022: in time; on 1 April 2023: too late.
#ASSERT `Is my request for reinstatement made in time and in writing (s 70.1(2); regulation 71)` (YearMonthDay 2022 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 31) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my request for reinstatement made in time and in writing (s 70.1(2); regulation 71)` (YearMonthDay 2022 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2023 4 1) TRUE)
-- Must the Minister approve? Born 15 June 1957 (65 in July 2022); ceased March 2021; incapable again 10 June 2022: yes. On 1 July 2022: no.
#ASSERT `Must the Minister approve my request for reinstatement (s 70.1(3))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2022 6 10) (YearMonthDay 1957 6 15) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister approve my request for reinstatement (s 70.1(3))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) (YearMonthDay 1957 6 15) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the Minister reinstate my child's disabled contributor's child benefit when my pension is reinstated (s 70.1(4))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister reinstate my child's disabled contributor's child benefit when my pension is reinstated (s 70.1(4))` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the Minister tell me in writing whether my request for reinstatement is approved (s 70.1(5))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister tell me in writing whether my request for reinstatement is approved (s 70.1(5))` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the Minister tell me in writing whether a disabled contributor's child benefit is approved on a reinstatement (s 70.1(6))` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister tell me in writing whether a disabled contributor's child benefit is approved on a reinstatement (s 70.1(6))` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The reinstated pension need not meet the contribution test again (paragraph 44(1)(b) does not apply), nor wait four months (section 69 does not).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does a provision of the Act apply to my reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit (s 70.1(7))` `the provision paragraph 44(1)(b)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does a provision of the Act apply to my reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit (s 70.1(7))` `the provision section 69`)
#ASSERT `Does a provision of the Act apply to my reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit (s 70.1(7))` `another provision of the Act`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does a provision of the Act apply to my reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit (s 70.1(8))` `the provision subsection 74(2)`)
#ASSERT `Does a provision of the Act apply to my reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit (s 70.1(8))` `the provision section 69`
-- The least amount: 900 against a calculated 800, no division: 900.
#ASSERT `How much is my reinstated disability pension, or the survivor's pension I receive, per month at least (s 70.1(9))` 800 900 FALSE EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `From which month is my reinstated pension or benefit paid (s 70.1(10))` (YearMonthDay 2021 12 12) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2022 1 1

§§ `Death benefit`

-- A contributor died on 10 January 2023 and nobody has applied for the estate; today is 20 March 2023 (the 60 days ended on 11 March): the Minister may direct payment.
#ASSERT `May the Minister direct the death benefit to someone other than the estate (s 71(2); regulation 64(1))` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2023 1 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2023 3 20) 5000 0
-- The estate applied on 11 March 2023, in time: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Minister direct the death benefit to someone other than the estate (s 71(2); regulation 64(1))` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2023 1 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 11) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 20) 5000 0)
#ASSERT `To whom is the death benefit paid (s 71)` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 1 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2023 3 20) 5000 0 EQUALS JUST `the death benefit is paid to a prescribed person or body as the Minister directs`
#ASSERT `To whom is the death benefit paid (s 71)` TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 1 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2023 3 20) 5000 0 EQUALS JUST `the death benefit is paid to the estate of the contributor`
#ASSERT `To whom is the death benefit paid (s 71)` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 1 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2023 3 20) 5000 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `To whom may the Minister direct the death benefit, in order (regulation 64(1))` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `payment is directed to the individual or institution who has paid or is responsible for the funeral expenses`
#ASSERT `To whom may the Minister direct the death benefit, in order (regulation 64(1))` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `payment is directed to the survivor of the deceased contributor`
#ASSERT `To whom may the Minister direct the death benefit, in order (regulation 64(1))` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `payment cannot be directed to anyone whom regulation 64(1) describes`
#ASSERT `How much of the death benefit can go to me if I paid the funeral expenses (regulation 64(2))` 2500 1000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I still claim the death benefit for the contributor's estate after it was paid to someone else under subsection 71(2) (s 71(3))` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Can I still claim the death benefit for the contributor's estate after it was paid to someone else under subsection 71(2) (s 71(3))` FALSE

§§ `Survivor's pension`

-- Noor, born 10 January 1970, 45 at the contributor's death on 20 March 2015; pension approved; entitled under (i); applied in June 2015: April 2015.
#ASSERT `From which month is my survivor's pension payable (s 72)` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1970 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2015 3 20) FALSE FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 4 1)
-- Applying late, in June 2017: not earlier than July 2016.
#ASSERT `From which month is my survivor's pension payable (s 72)` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1970 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2015 3 20) FALSE FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2017 6 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 7 1)
#ASSERT `From which month is my survivor's pension payable (s 72)` FALSE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1970 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2015 3 20) FALSE FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 10) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 73: a division approved effective June 2023 ends the pension with that month.
#ASSERT `Is my survivor's pension paid for a particular month (s 73)` (YearMonthDay 2023 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 1 1) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 6 15) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2021 2 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my survivor's pension paid for a particular month (s 73)` (YearMonthDay 2023 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 1 1) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 6 15) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2021 2 1))
#ASSERT `Is my survivor's pension safe when a pension is approved for the contributor's common-law partner (s 73(2))` (YearMonthDay 2000 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2000 7 31) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my survivor's pension safe when a pension is approved for the contributor's common-law partner (s 73(2))` (YearMonthDay 1997 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2000 7 31) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does my survivor's pension end because of a division of pensionable earnings (s 73(3))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 6 15) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2021 2 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 6 1)
-- A new conjugal relationship of more than a year at the contributor's death: the pension does not end.
#ASSERT `Does my survivor's pension end because of a division of pensionable earnings (s 73(3))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 6 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 2 1) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Disabled contributor's child's benefit and orphan's benefit`

#ASSERT `May I apply for the child's or orphan's benefit on the child's behalf (s 74(1))` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I apply for the child's or orphan's benefit on the child's behalf (s 74(1))` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `From which month is the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable (s 74(2)(a))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2019 1 12) (YearMonthDay 2020 9 5) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 8 1)
#ASSERT `From which month is the orphan's benefit payable (s 74(2)(b))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 2 2) (YearMonthDay 2021 5 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1)
-- A benefit already payable in respect of another contributor, who is not a parent: barred; a parent: not barred.
#ASSERT `Is the child's or orphan's benefit barred in respect of this contributor (s 74(3))` TRUE FALSE 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the child's or orphan's benefit barred in respect of this contributor (s 74(3))` TRUE TRUE 1)
-- A child born 15 June 2010, asked about on 30 June 2025: someone with decision-making responsibility is paid; on 1 July 2028 the child has reached 18 and the subsection is silent.
#ASSERT `To whom is the child's or orphan's benefit paid (s 75(1))` (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) TRUE EQUALS JUST `the benefit is paid to the person or agency having decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan`
#ASSERT `To whom is the child's or orphan's benefit paid (s 75(1))` (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) FALSE EQUALS JUST `the benefit is paid to the person or agency the Minister directs`
#ASSERT `To whom is the child's or orphan's benefit paid (s 75(1))` (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2028 7 1) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Who is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan (s 75(2))` FALSE FALSE FALSE 60 EQUALS `the contributor is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child`
#ASSERT `Who is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan (s 75(2))` TRUE FALSE TRUE 50 EQUALS `the survivor of the contributor is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the orphan`
-- The child's benefit ends with the month the child ceases to be a dependent child (December 2025) when that is the earliest event.
#ASSERT `Until which month is the disabled contributor's child's benefit paid (s 76(1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 3) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE 0 0 FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1)
-- Adopted by a stranger in June 2025, the contributor not maintaining the child: June 2025.
#ASSERT `Until which month is the disabled contributor's child's benefit paid (s 76(1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 3) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 14) FALSE 0 0 FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1)
-- ... but if the contributor makes periodic provision of at least the benefit ($350), the adoption does not end it.
#ASSERT `Until which month is the disabled contributor's child's benefit paid (s 76(1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 12 3) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 14) TRUE 400 350 FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1)
-- No event yet: not covered.
#ASSERT `Until which month is the disabled contributor's child's benefit paid (s 76(1))` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE 0 0 FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Until which month is the orphan's benefit paid (s 76(2))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 6 30) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 9) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 6 1)
#ASSERT `In which month is my application for an orphan's benefit treated as made when a disabled contributor's child's benefit ceases because of the contributor's death (s 76(3))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2000 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2019 2 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 2 1)
#ASSERT `In which month is my application for an orphan's benefit treated as made when a disabled contributor's child's benefit ceases because of the contributor's death (s 76(3))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2001 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2019 2 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Post-retirement benefit`

#ASSERT `From which month will I receive a post-retirement benefit for my earnings (s 76.1)` TRUE TRUE 10000 3500 (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) 2024 EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1)
#ASSERT `From which month will I receive a post-retirement benefit for my earnings (s 76.1)` TRUE TRUE 3500 3500 (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) 2024 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Until which month is the post-retirement benefit paid (s 76.2)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 8 1)
#ASSERT `Until which month is the post-retirement benefit paid (s 76.2)` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `The share paid under the Canada Pension Plan`

-- Totals of 30000, 3000 and 0 under the Act against 40000, 4000 and 1000 in all: 33000 / 45000 = 11 / 15.
#ASSERT `What proportion of my benefit is paid under the Canada Pension Plan (s 77)` 30000 3000 0 40000 4000 1000 EQUALS JUST (11 DIVIDED BY 15)
#ASSERT `What proportion of my benefit is paid under the Canada Pension Plan (s 77)` 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How much of my monthly benefit is paid under the Canada Pension Plan, in dollars (ss 77 and 80)` 1000 TRUE 0.75 `no agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under one plan` EQUALS JUST 750
#ASSERT `How much of my monthly benefit is paid under the Canada Pension Plan, in dollars (ss 77 and 80)` 1000 TRUE 0.75 `an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under this Act` EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `How much of my monthly benefit is paid under the Canada Pension Plan, in dollars (ss 77 and 80)` 1000 TRUE 0.75 `an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under the provincial pension plan` EQUALS JUST 0
-- 30000 under the Act and 10000 under a provincial plan in a year: three quarters; a year of a division with 20000 attributed of 50000: two fifths.
#ASSERT `What share of my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78 and 79)` 30000 10000 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0.75
#ASSERT `What share of my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78 and 79)` 30000 10000 TRUE 20000 50000 EQUALS JUST 0.4
#ASSERT `What share of my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78.1 and 79.1)` 30000 10000 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0.75
#ASSERT `What share of my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78.1 and 79.1)` 30000 10000 TRUE 20000 50000 EQUALS JUST 0.4
#ASSERT `What share of my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78.2 and 79.2)` 30000 10000 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0.75
#ASSERT `What share of my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78.2 and 79.2)` 0 0 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the agreement that apportions my disability benefit within the limits the Act sets (s 80.1(4))` FALSE FALSE 400 300 600
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the agreement that apportions my disability benefit within the limits the Act sets (s 80.1(4))` FALSE FALSE 200 300 600)
#ASSERT `How much disability benefit is payable under the Canada Pension Plan for the month when an agreement applies to me (s 80.1(3))` TRUE TRUE 400 600 EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `How much disability benefit is payable under the Canada Pension Plan for the month when an agreement applies to me (s 80.1(3))` TRUE FALSE 700 600 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Reconsideration and appeal`

#ASSERT `May I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision or determination (s 81(1))` `an applicant dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(b)` `a decision made under section 60 that subsection 81(1) names` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision or determination (s 81(1))` `an applicant dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(b)` `a decision made under section 65.1 that subsection 81(1) names` TRUE)
#ASSERT `May someone else make the request for reconsideration for me (s 81(1))` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I notified of the decision in the way the regulations require (s 81(1); regulation 74.2)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I notified of the decision in the way the regulations require (s 81(1); regulation 74.2)` TRUE FALSE)
-- Notified on 10 January 2023: the 90 days end on 10 April 2023.
#ASSERT `By what day must I ask the Minister to reconsider (s 81(1) and (1.1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 1 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 4 10)
#ASSERT `By what day must I ask the Minister to reconsider (s 81(1) and (1.1))` FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my request for reconsideration made in time (s 81(1) and (1.1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 1 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2023 4 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my request for reconsideration made in time (s 81(1) and (1.1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 1 10) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` (YearMonthDay 2023 4 11))
#ASSERT `Is my request for reconsideration made in time (s 81(1) and (1.1))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 1 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 6 30) (YearMonthDay 2023 6 30)
#ASSERT `May the Minister allow me a longer period to ask for reconsideration (s 81(1); regulation 74.1(3) and (4))` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Minister allow me a longer period to ask for reconsideration (s 81(1); regulation 74.1(3) and (4))` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is my request for reconsideration in the form the regulations require (s 81(1); regulation 74.1(1))` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my request for reconsideration in the form the regulations require (s 81(1); regulation 74.1(1))` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May I ask the Minister to reconsider the penalty assessed on me (s 81(1.1))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `What must the Minister do and tell me after I ask for a reconsideration (s 81(2))` TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Minister rescind or amend a decision made about me (s 81(3))` TRUE
#ASSERT `May I appeal the Minister's decision on my reconsideration to the Social Security Tribunal (s 82)` TRUE
#ASSERT `Until what day may the Minister stay payment of my benefit after a Tribunal decision (s 83)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 9 30) (YearMonthDay 2023 10 30) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 10 30)
#ASSERT `Until what day may the Minister stay payment of my benefit after a Tribunal decision (s 83)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 9 30) (YearMonthDay 2023 10 30) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 3 12) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 3 31)
#ASSERT `Until what day may the Minister stay payment of my benefit after a Tribunal decision (s 83)` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2023 9 30) (YearMonthDay 2023 10 30) FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Census information and presumed death`

-- A census taken on 31 May 1990 and a request on 1 June 2020: more than thirty years; a census on 1 June 1990: exactly thirty, not more.
#ASSERT `May the Minister get my age from old census returns (s 87; regulation 51)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1990 5 31) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Minister get my age from old census returns (s 87; regulation 51)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1990 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- A contributor disappeared; in the Minister's opinion the circumstances raise the presumption; the Minister determined 5 May 2020.
#ASSERT `From which date is a contributor, beneficiary or spouse of mine who has disappeared treated as having died (s 88(1))` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 5 5) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 5 5)
#ASSERT `From which date is a contributor, beneficiary or spouse of mine who has disappeared treated as having died (s 88(1))` TRUE TRUE FALSE `cp5 case -- a day that is not used` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `From which date is the person treated as having died once the Minister determines a different date (s 88(2))` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1)
#ASSERT `Must the Minister pay me the benefit I would have been paid had the death not been presumed (s 88(2) and (3))` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the Minister pay me the benefit I would have been paid had the death not been presumed (s 88(2) and (3))` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Minister pay me the benefit I would have been paid had the death not been presumed (s 88(2) and (3))` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must a benefit paid to me because another person was presumed dead stop once the Minister is satisfied that person is alive (s 88(4))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I keep what I was paid before the Minister was satisfied that the other person is alive (s 88(4))` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does a death certificate issued or revoked by another authority bind the Minister in deciding on my benefit (s 88(5))` TRUE)

§§ `False statements, offences and penalties`

#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence under the Act by what I said or did (s 90(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I committed an offence under the Act by what I said or did (s 90(1))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The Minister became aware on 10 March 2020: proceedings may be started until 10 March 2025.
#ASSERT `By what day can proceedings be started against me for an offence (s 90(2))` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 10) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 3 10
#ASSERT `Can proceedings still be started against me for the offence on a given day (s 90(2))` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can proceedings still be started against me for the offence on a given day (s 90(2))` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 11))
#ASSERT `Am I protected from prosecution for an act or omission for which a penalty was imposed on me (s 90(3))` TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Minister impose a penalty on me for what I said or did (s 90.1(1))` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister impose a penalty on me for what I said or did (s 90.1(1))` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `What is the most the Minister can set as the penalty on me, in dollars (s 90.1(2))` 3 EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT `Is the penalty set on me within the maximum for each act or omission (s 90.1(2))` 10000
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the penalty set on me within the maximum for each act or omission (s 90.1(2))` 10000.01)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it too late for the Minister to impose a penalty on me (s 90.1(3))` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 9))
#ASSERT `Is it too late for the Minister to impose a penalty on me (s 90.1(3))` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10)
#ASSERT `Is it too late for the Minister to impose a penalty on me (s 90.1(3))` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister rescind or reduce the penalty imposed on me (s 90.1(4))` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Minister rescind or reduce the penalty imposed on me (s 90.1(4))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

